<title>USA: Sagebrush buys back 375,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Sagebrush buys back 375,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>CLAREMONT, N.C. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sagebrush Inc said Friday that it has repurchased 375,000 shares of its common stock in a negotiated block purchase from an institutional investor at a price of $5.25 per share.</p>
<p>The company said that the purchase will not impair its ability to finance continued growth, and believes that it will have a positive effect on per share earnings.</p>
<p>Sagebrush shares closed Monday at 6-1/8.</p>
<p>The company owns and operates 29 restaurants in North Carolina, South Carolina, Tennessee and Virginia, which serve moderately-priced meals in a casual, family-oriented atmosphere.</p>
</text>
